19	Important update: Testing Vendor Transition in Progress
20	Eﬀective March 1, 2026, the IRS Enrolled Agent Special Enrollment Exam (EA-SEE) is no
21	longer developed and administered by Prometric, LLC. A new vendor, PSI Services, has been
22	selected to develop and administer the exam.
23	
24	Registration and scheduling for the 2026 EA-SEE test cycle are now open. Candidates can
25	register and schedule appointments through PSI Services.
26	
27	
28	Steps to becoming an enrolled agent:
29	 1. Obtain a preparer tax identification number (PTIN).
30	 2. Visit PSI’s Special Enrollment Examination (SEE)  webpage to schedule your test
31	    appointments, review the SEE Candidate Information Bulletin , sample test
32	    questions, and other test preparation resources. Achieve passing scores on all three
33	    parts of the SEE within three years.
34	 3. Apply for enrollment and pay enrollment fee electronically using Pay.gov Form 23  or
35	    by downloading Form 23, Application for Enrollment to Practice Before the Internal
36	    Revenue Service PDF and mailing the completed form and a check to the IRS.
37	 4. Pass a suitability check, which will include tax compliance to ensure that you have filed
38	    all necessary tax returns and there are no outstanding tax liabilities, and criminal
39	    background.
40	
41	*Certain IRS employees, by virtue of past technical experience, are exempt from the exam
42	requirement.
43	
44	
45	Once you become an enrolled agent you must:
46	   Renew your status as an enrolled agent every three years
47	   Obtain continuing education
48	   Renew your PTIN annually
